14. Interview Questions
=======================

Q1. What is template specialization?

Providing a custom implementation of a template for specific data types.

---------------------------------------------------------

Q2. Why do we need specialization?

To optimize or customize behavior for particular types.

---------------------------------------------------------

Q3. What is full specialization?

A specialization for one exact type.

Example

Printer<bool>

---------------------------------------------------------

Q4. What is partial specialization?

Specializing only some template parameters.

Example

Pair<T,int>

---------------------------------------------------------

Q5. Which templates support partial specialization?

✓ Class Templates

✗ Function Templates

---------------------------------------------------------

Q6. Why can't function templates be partially specialized?

Because function overloading provides the required functionality.

---------------------------------------------------------

Q7. Which specialization has the highest priority?

Priority Order

1. Full Specialization

2. Partial Specialization

3. Generic Template

---------------------------------------------------------

Q8. Can member functions be specialized?

Yes.

---------------------------------------------------------

Q9. Is specialization decided at compile time?

Yes.

---------------------------------------------------------

Q10. Give STL examples of template specialization.

• std::vector<bool>

